      "problem": "The solution to the inequality $-10x-13<17$ is$\\,x$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}.",
      "worked_solution": "First, we apply the addition principle, adding $13$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-10x-13 & <17 \\\\ -10x-13+13 & <17+13 \\\\ -10x+0 & <30 \\\\ -10x & <30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by $-10.$ \n\nRemember, when multiplying or dividing an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-10x\\,\\, & <\\,\\,30 \\\\ \\frac{-10x}{-10}\\, & >\\,\\,\\frac{30}{-10} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{-10}x}{\\cancel{-10}}\\, & >\\,\\,-3 \\\\ x\\,\\, & >\\,-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x>-3.$",
